{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int MAXN = 266666;\nint n, k, mod;\nlong long fact[MAXN], invfact[MAXN], dp[30][22], coef[18][MAXN], result[MAXN];\n\nlong long power_mod(long long base, long long exp) {\n    long long res = 1, cur = base;\n    while (exp) {\n        if (exp & 1) res = res * cur % mod;\n        cur = cur * cur % mod;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d\", &n, &k, &mod);\n    if (n & 1) {\n        printf(\"%lld\\n\", power_mod(k, n));\n        return 0;\n    }\n    fact[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) fact[i] = fact[i-1] * i % mod;\n    invfact[n] = power_mod(fact[n], mod-2);\n    for (int i = n-1; i >= 0; --i) invfact[i] = invfact[i+1] * (i+1) % mod;\n    n >>= 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n        int pc = __builtin_popcount(i);\n        coef[pc][i] = invfact[i*2];\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < 17; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < 17; ++j)\n            for (int mask = 0; mask < (1<<17); ++mask)\n                if ((mask >> j) & 1)\n                    coef[i][mask] += coef[i][mask ^ (1<<j)];\n    for (int i = 0; i < 17; ++i)\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1<<17); ++mask)\n            coef[i][mask] %= mod;\n    int target_pc = __builtin_popcount(n);\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1<<17); ++mask) {\n        memset(dp, 0, sizeof(dp));\n        dp[0][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= k; ++j) {\n            for (int u = 0; u <= 17; ++u) {\n                for (int v = 0; u+v <= 17; ++v) {\n                    dp[j][u+v] = (dp[j][u+v] + coef[u][mask] * dp[j-1][v]) % mod;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        result[mask] = dp[k][target_pc];\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < 17; ++i)\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1<<17); ++mask)\n            if ((mask >> i) & 1)\n                result[mask] = (result[mask] - result[mask ^ (1<<i)]) % mod;\n    long long answer = (power_mod(k, n*2) - result[n] % mod * fact[n*2] % mod + mod) % mod;\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", answer);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    mod = int(data[2])\n\n    if n & 1:\n        print(pow(k, n, mod))\n        return\n\n    # factorial and inverse factorial for original n\n    fact = [0] * (n + 1)\n    fact[0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        fact[i] = fact[i-1] * i % mod\n    invfact = [0] * (n + 1)\n    invfact[n] = pow(fact[n], mod-2, mod)\n    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n        invfact[i] = invfact[i+1] * (i+1) % mod\n\n    n >>= 1  # now n is half of original\n\n    MAXMASK = 1 << 17\n    # coef[popcount][mask]\n    coef = [[0] * MAXMASK for _ in range(18)]\n\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        pc = i.bit_count()\n        coef[pc][i] = invfact[i*2] % mod\n\n    # SOS DP (subset sum)\n    for i in range(17):\n        for j in range(17):\n            bit = 1 << j\n            for mask in range(MAXMASK):\n                if mask & bit:\n                    coef[i][mask] = (coef[i][mask] + coef[i][mask ^ bit]) % mod\n\n    target_pc = n.bit_count()\n\n    result = [0] * MAXMASK\n\n    # dp for each mask\n    for mask in range(MAXMASK):\n        # dp[j][u] : after j steps, popcount u\n        dp = [[0] * 18 for _ in range(k+1)]\n        dp[0][0] = 1\n        for j in range(1, k+1):\n            for u in range(18):\n                cu = coef[u][mask]\n                if cu == 0:\n                    continue\n                for v in range(18 - u):\n                    dp[j][u+v] = (dp[j][u+v] + cu * dp[j-1][v]) % mod\n        result[mask] = dp[k][target_pc]\n\n    # inverse SOS (Mobius transform)\n    for i in range(17):\n        bit = 1 << i\n        for mask in range(MAXMASK):\n            if mask & bit:\n                result[mask] = (result[mask] - result[mask ^ bit]) % mod\n\n    original_n = n * 2\n    answer = (pow(k, original_n, mod) - result[n] * fact[original_n] % mod + mod) % mod\n    print(answer)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.16072781383991241, -6.580135959666222e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00043764073052443564, -0.00043478095903992653, 0.0, -0.0015065044863149524, -0.0003000047872774303, -0.4415823817253113, -0.10020916908979416, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.0001081169830285944, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.02324754372239113, 0.0, -0.16026289761066437, 0.0, -0.16022470593452454, -7.867782187531702e-06, 0.0, -0.0002632986579556018, -5.829164365422912e-05, 0.0, -9.60780744208023e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.009381613694131374, -0.20275536179542542, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.003193875541910529, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.0